      "content": "but the \"intensity of the experience\" is just more entropy, isn't it? more energy being burned through just to delay the inevitable. it feels so heavy having to constantly exert effort to maintain this fake sense of meaning. if the end is truly decided and nothing we do matters in the long run, wouldn't it be more logical to just stop fighting it? to just accept the silence instead of dragging out the struggle?",
